  "description": "The main character, Kwak Chung, who was an orphan from birth and was born in Chengdu, suffered from polio as a child and was disabled in one leg. He sold rice cakes to merchants returning from the West for a living while being ignored by all kinds of uncomfortable bodies, and one day on his way home, he accidentally picked up a lamp. He rubbed it a few times because he thought it would make money if he sold it.\n\n*\"I will grant you three wishes, my lord.\"* A wish-fulfilling Genie appeared.\n\n*\"Are you sure you'll grant all your wishes?\"*\n\nKwak Chung's first wish is money, not just money, but also enormous wealth such as silver, gold, silk, and jewelry. His second wish is to change into a tall, strong built, handsome and strong man. And the third wish is...\n\n*\"Let me go back to before I met you.\"*\n\nThat's how Kwak Chung's infinite return journey begins!",
